Accidental local reset|A developer moved the branch tip and cannot find a committed change.|git reflog --date=iso -20|Locate the prior tip and inspect the commit before changing refs. Distinguish committed work from uncommitted content, which reflog may not recover.|Create a recovery branch at the verified commit, then integrate deliberately. Avoid more destructive cleanup until useful work is preserved.|Compare recovered files and run relevant tests; confirm no collaborator history was overwritten.
Published bad commit|A merged commit introduces a production regression.|git show --stat BAD_COMMIT|Identify the change and later dependencies; compare code rollback with current schema and external effects.|Create a reviewed revert when compatible, or a forward fix when reversal would damage data. Preserve shared history rather than force-resetting main.|Run regression tests and verify production behavior after deploying the chosen recovery artifact.
Merge conflict hides logic loss|Conflict markers are removed but one branch's behavior is missing.|git diff --staged|Review the common intent of both changes and inspect surrounding code, not only the marked lines.|Resolve the semantic combination explicitly and add or run a test covering both requirements. Abort and restart the integration if the resolution is unclear.|Verify both original behaviors and the combined path before committing the merge result.
CI passes but deployment differs|The deployed application does not match the revision that passed tests.|git log --oneline -10|Trace source commit, build artifact digest and deployment record. Check whether a later rebuild or mutable tag substituted different bytes.|Promote the tested immutable artifact and bind deployment gates to its digest. Correct the pipeline's source-to-artifact evidence.|Verify the running artifact digest and expected behavior, then test that a changed artifact cannot bypass the gate.
Secret committed to repository|A credential appears in a commit and CI logs.|git show --stat AFFECTED_COMMIT|Identify the credential's exposure, readers, artifacts and active uses without printing it again. Removing the latest file does not invalidate prior copies.|Revoke or rotate the credential first, repair consumers and follow the repository's history/artifact cleanup procedure. Add appropriate secret prevention checks.|Confirm the old credential is unusable, consumers use the replacement and future test commits are detected before publication.
Flaky test blocks releases|The same revision alternates between pass and failure.|git log --oneline -- PATH_TO_TEST|Compare failure signatures, timing, shared resources and test order. Determine whether the flake masks an actual product race.|Fix isolation or synchronization; if temporary quarantine is necessary, assign an owner and expiry while preserving critical coverage elsewhere.|Run the meaningful reproduction repeatedly under varied order/load and confirm stable results without unlimited retries.
Concurrent deployments collide|Two CI jobs update the same environment and leave mixed versions.|git log --oneline -10|Compare deployment timestamps, artifact identities and shared-state changes. Check whether cancellation left a partially applied operation.|Serialize per-environment deployments and reconcile to one known-good artifact. Define safe cancellation and recovery for partial updates.|Run overlapping test deployments and verify only one writer operates while final environment state matches a single recorded release.
Dependency update breaks builds|A build fails without application-source changes.|git diff BASE_COMMIT HEAD -- package-lock.json|Inspect lock-file changes, toolchain versions, mutable references and cache keys. A stale cache can also obscure the actual dependency set.|Pin reproducible inputs, invalidate the affected cache appropriately and test the dependency update separately. Do not broadly downgrade unrelated packages.|Build from a clean environment and verify the same inputs produce the intended tested artifact.
OIDC credential exchange denied|A deployment job cannot obtain its cloud role credentials.|git show HEAD:.github/workflows/deploy.yml|Inspect the job identity-token permission, audience and trust-policy subject conditions. Repository, branch or environment identity may differ from the allowed context.|Correct the narrow workflow permission or trust condition for the intended release path. Do not allow every repository or pull request to assume the deployment role.|Test the authorized job and confirm an untrusted branch or repository remains denied.
Regression origin unclear|A bug exists on main but the introducing commit is unknown.|git log --oneline -- PATH|Choose verified good and bad revisions and a deterministic reproduction. Confirm unrelated build failures can be distinguished from the bug.|Use controlled bisection with the reproduction, inspect the identified change and create a focused fix. Preserve local work before changing checkouts.|Run the reproduction against the parent, culprit and fix and verify neighboring behavior remains correct.
